    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "About one hundred years ago, on October 10, 1925, the Forbidden City in Beijing threw open its golden gates to the public. It was no longer the secret world of emperors but became the Palace Museum. Anyone could walk through the halls where history was made. And today, it is the world’s most visited museum, attracting almost 20 million visitors every year."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Have you ever stepped inside the Palace Museum? Once you do, you will find yourself at the heart of one of the richest cultural collections on Earth. More than 1.8 million artefacts are displayed or stored there. Ancient "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "bronzes",
            "zh": "青铜器"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "jade carvings",
            "zh": "玉雕"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", calligraphy works, and paintings hundreds of years old line the halls. Each item is like a quiet storyteller. They show visitors how people in China once lived, what they created, and what they believed in. As you gaze at the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "porcelain",
            "zh": "瓷器"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "dragon robes",
            "zh": "龙袍"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", golden treasures, and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "imperial armour",
            "zh": "御甲"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", you won’t just admire them but begin to understand them: These are not just priceless artefacts; they are “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "threads",
            "zh": "丝线"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” tying you back to a culture that has "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "thrived",
            "ref": "v-thrive"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for over 5,000 years."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Beyond its treasures, the Palace Museum itself is a wonder. The former Forbidden City is the world’s largest standing wooden palace "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "complex",
            "zh": "建筑群"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Its red walls, golden roofs, grand gates, and large courtyards show the beauty of balance and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "harmony",
            "ref": "v-harmony"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "—two "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "concepts",
            "ref": "v-concept"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " central to Chinese "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "philosophy",
            "zh": "哲学"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Only by walking through its grounds can you truly appreciate the thought and power behind its design."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The Palace Museum keeps reminding us why history must be kept alive. Each part of it and each of its artefacts carries a message across time. They invite us to listen, learn, and connect with a culture that has shaped human history. The museum has amazed countless visitors, and it’s still calling us to step through its gates and discover more about China’s past."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
